From: Mo Werk <mo@mowerk.net>
Date: Sun, 17 Aug 2026 01:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] amplifiers: cs40l26-codec: report state to monaco-asoc

sol has no sound card at all: monaco-asoc-snd never creates one, retrying
forever with

    populate_snd_card_dailinks(): CS40L26 codec support present
        - Using Primary MI2S | snd_cs40l26_loaded: 0
    msm_asoc_machine_probe: Card uninitialized
    msm_asoc_machine_probe: Defer probe for card retry

monaco.c gates the card on a tri-state that the codec is expected to write:

    == 1   add the haptics DAI links
    == 0   card_defer_probe = true; return NULL
    else   skip haptics, bring the card up anyway

snd_cs40l26_loaded is defined and exported by machine_dlkm itself
(asoc/monaco.c). The codec half is what sets it -- and only in the seluna
generation of this driver (cs40l26-codec.c:19,1153,1159 there), which is what
sol's audio module was written against. sol builds amplifiers from the
pixel-watch branch instead, because seluna's is bazel-only, and that branch
has no writer anywhere in the tree. So the flag stays 0 and the card defers
forever.

Note this is NOT the same symbol as cs40l26_loaded, the bool externed from
cs40l26.c just above: that one gates this probe, this one gates the sound
card. Two similarly named flags, only one of which had a writer here.

Mirror seluna's semantics exactly: 1 once the component registers, -1 on any
failure return, so a codec that cannot come up degrades to a card without the
haptics DAI rather than no card at all.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [sol-specific: pairs a pixel-watch-branch
codec with a seluna-branch audio module]

Signed-off-by: Mo Werk <mo@mowerk.net>
---
 .../google-modules/amplifiers/cs40l26/cs40l26-codec.c  | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/private/google-modules/amplifiers/cs40l26/cs40l26-codec.c b/private/google-modules/amplifiers/cs40l26/cs40l26-codec.c
--- a/private/google-modules/amplifiers/cs40l26/cs40l26-codec.c
+++ b/private/google-modules/amplifiers/cs40l26/cs40l26-codec.c
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 };
 
 extern bool cs40l26_loaded;
+extern int snd_cs40l26_loaded;
 
 static int cs40l26_get_clk_config(u32 freq, u8 *clk_cfg)
 {
@@ -978,13 +979,16 @@
 	if (!cs40l26_loaded) {
 		/* cs40l26 did not load successfully */
 		dev_err(&pdev->dev, "Skipping cs40l26-codec probe\n");
+		snd_cs40l26_loaded = -1;
 		return -EIO;
 	}
 
 	codec = devm_kzalloc(&pdev->dev, sizeof(struct cs40l26_codec),
 			GFP_KERNEL);
-	if (!codec)
+	if (!codec) {
+		snd_cs40l26_loaded = -1;
 		return -ENOMEM;
+	}
 
 	codec->core = cs40l26;
 	codec->regmap = cs40l26->regmap;
@@ -996,8 +1000,12 @@
 
 	ret = snd_soc_register_component(&pdev->dev, &soc_codec_dev_cs40l26,
 			cs40l26_dai, ARRAY_SIZE(cs40l26_dai));
-	if (ret < 0)
+	if (ret < 0) {
 		dev_err(&pdev->dev, "Failed to register codec: %d\n", ret);
+		snd_cs40l26_loaded = -1;
+	} else {
+		snd_cs40l26_loaded = 1;
+	}
 
 	return ret;
 }
